  "question": {
    "text": "The mean square deviation of a set of observations&nbsp;<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msub></math> about a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is defined as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo stretchy=\"true\">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></munderover><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.&nbsp;If the mean square deviations about <math><mo>–</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><mn>1</mn></math> of a set of observations are <math><mn>7</mn></math> and <math><mn>3</mn></math> respectively. The standard deviation of those observations is"
